# Example clarity (lunch-marcoly)

A major **goal** is concise, clear examples that teach one idea well.

## Preludes on functions and methods

- Prefer short, well-documented preludes (docstrings / block comments) on public functions and methods.
- **Emphasize** preludes where LaunchDarkly will be inserted or is already wired — name the LD surface the reader should notice (flag evaluation, context, AI Config, etc.).
- Keep preludes instructional, not essay-length: what this does, why LD belongs here, what to look at next.

```text
✅ GOOD — points at the LD insertion site
# Evaluate the feature flag before choosing the nav label.
# LaunchDarkly: boolean flag variation — see docs link at call site.

❌ BAD — silence at the LD boundary, or a novel above every helper
```

## Instrumenting with LaunchDarkly

When adding or documenting LD instrumentation in code or READMEs:

1. **Link** to the official LaunchDarkly documentation for that topic.
2. Include **keywords** that name the capability (e.g. *feature flags*, *boolean variations*, *contexts*, *segments*, *AI Config*, *Experimentation*, *Guarded rollout*).
3. Prefer one sharp link + keywords over a dump of unrelated docs.

Example shape (adapt URL to the current LD docs page for the topic):

```text
# Feature flags — boolean variation
# https://docs.launchdarkly.com/home/flags/boolean
```

## Scope vs noise

- Document the LD-relevant path thoroughly; leave trivial getters/formatters lightly commented.
- Match existing language idioms (Python docstrings, JSDoc, Go doc comments, etc.).
- Do not paste secrets, SDK keys, or project-specific dashboard URLs into shared examples.
